# Development and Decision Ledger

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Entire v1 lifecycle
Dependencies: None

## Purpose

Preserve instructions, decisions, evidence, corrections, and cross-session ownership without invented progress.

## Tasks

- [x] Record the initial research/planning scope and absence of application code.
- [x] Record Windows 11-first approval and the separate four-product qualification requirement.
- [x] Record the recurring numbered TODO convention and limits of the bounded cross-project survey.
- [x] Separate source research, proposed architecture, implemented behavior, and release qualification.
- [ ] Append significant decision/implementation/validation/owner-review milestones as they happen.
- [ ] Record blockers, superseded/rejected approaches, exact candidate identities, and claim changes.
- [ ] Keep index/task/docs and designated private context synchronized at milestones.
- [ ] Close with final v1 handoff evidence; retain deferred work without implying it blocks the release.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Every v1 milestone has a dated source-grounded record and an honest current status.
- [ ] Human approval is distinguished from technical success.
- [ ] No real notes, private credentials, unrelated sibling work, or personal capture evidence is published.
- [ ] Final handoff identifies remaining support boundaries and maintenance ownership.

## Completion evidence

- Planning documents and task catalogue are the only current project artifacts.
- Local session context registration/offload is separate from app implementation and public source.

